# Inputs for the hash-locked requirements.lock: the runtime dependencies of
# open-terminal at OPEN_TERMINAL_VERSION (from its pyproject.toml) that apply
# on Linux, its "notebooks" extra (nbclient, ipykernel: notebook support, which
# v0.14.0 had built in), plus hatchling, its build backend, so the verified
# checkout builds without fetching anything unhashed. Left out on purpose:
# pyautogui, which only drives the machine's own screen (host desktop mode,
# loaded lazily) and ships as source only, with six source-only dependencies;
# the CT has no display and the workspaces run with the desktop off
# (OMITTED_DEPS in install-target.sh). The one lock must resolve identically
# on Python 3.11 (Debian 12) and 3.13 (Debian 13); regenerate and compare it
# as targets/open-terminal/README.md describes ("Updating the pin").
